From dcb3f35c0860cfc408896abe121b01b6d2689f26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:21:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 1.4.0: the pulse gone, the plate and the genes at 22 kHz, the
 reel's modulators, init and undo

- the pulse (its thump and hats, its page, its rings on the screen, its MIDI) gone: three voices; SEQ opens the reel,
  again its next page; the fourth level bar the reel's
- less work: the plate at 22.05 kHz (its lines half: 35 KB of the pool back), the reel's genes at the tape's own rate,
  each an output pair's line: on the PC, 60 s of four genes 0.96 s -> 0.74 s
- the reel's two modulators (Tape Mod 1, 2): a target of its ten settings, depth, rate, shape; moving the setting as it
  plays and records; MIDI CC 62..69 on channel 16
- each piece its own modulation (each voice's second modulator, the reel's first), so a piece changed is heard
- SEL + SAVE initialises what the page is part of (a voice's modulators, how it plays, the reel, every modulator); SEL
  held undoes it, and the recipe (SAVE held) too
- project format 12 (11 and 10 carried over, the reel's source the mix where it was the pulse)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
